 introduced by #109971.\n\n### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in v4.6.dev.gh [78d91947f]\n- Reproducible in v4.6.dev3.official [9d84f3d13]\n- Reproducible in ec62f12862c4cfc76526eaf99afa0a24249f8288 (after #109971)\n- NOT Reproducible in 70f07467bed9cb7952b5523a720fba33bc7abf0e (before #109971)\n- NOT reproducible in v4.6.dev2.official [7864ac801]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.dev (78d91947f) - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Direct3D 12 (Mobile) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8088) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 61.64 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen using HDR 2D with the Mobile renderer and either the vulkan or d3d12 driver, the sky background of 3d environments appears dark:\n\nHDR 2D| Mobile | Forward+\n--|--|--\nEnabled | <img width=\"1796\" height=\"1104\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8f269169-439f-4087-8083-0ca56d70f414\" /> | <img width=\"1796\" height=\"1104\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f7af3e21-d6e5-4967-8d5b-c735e036f091\" />\nDisabled | <img width=\"1796\" height=\"1104\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a3ae0f20-8a86-4d3c-9a79-a57a7a080afa\" /> | <img width=\"1796\" height=\"1104\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fd0f61bb-b01e-4c34-95ef-c2631bc64d36\" />\n\nThis issue is described in more detail in this [comment from clayjohn](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/113897#issuecomment-3644450479); with the Mobile renderer, a different luminance multiplier must be used when rendering to a radiance map (2.0) vs. rendering to a viewport (1.0 for HDR 2D, 2.0 otherwise).\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a project\n2. Set HDR 2D to enabled\n3. See that Sky colour of 3D environment is too dark\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[mobile-black-3d.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23944710/mobile-black-3d.zip)"